# --- Overdue reminder emails ------------------------------------------------
# The daily job at /api/cron/reminders, scheduled in vercel.json. It chases
# unpaid TMS rent, and tells Micana owners and factory introducers when money
# we owe them is late. None of these are NEXT_PUBLIC — they must never reach
# the browser.
#
# NOTHING IS SENT unless REMINDERS_ENABLED is exactly "true". Leave it unset
# and the job still runs, still records what it would have done in
# reminder_log, and mails nobody. Read that table before turning it on.

# Vercel sets this header on scheduled invocations; the route rejects anything
# that does not present it. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32

# Authenticates the job to Postgres, the way a device key authenticates the
# aircon ingest — which is why no service-role key is needed here either.
# Generate one, put it here, and register its hash once:
#   insert into public.reminder_jobs (job_name, key_hash)
#   values ('overdue-reminders', encode(digest('<the key>','sha256'),'hex'));

# Resend.

# Who the mail comes from.
#
# Only the DOMAIN has to be verified with the mail provider; the display name
# in front of it is free text. That distinction is doing real work here, because
# only mcnasset.com is verified while the tenant is asked to pay Micana
# Innovation Sdn Bhd. A payment request whose sender and payee disagree is what
# people are told to be suspicious of, so the address stays on the verified
# domain and the name is the payee, written out exactly as the
# payment line in the same email writes it:
#
#   REMINDER_FROM_TMS_RENT="Micana Innovation Sdn Bhd <billing@mcnasset.com>"
#   REMINDER_FROM_MICANA_PAYOUT="Micana Innovation Sdn Bhd <billing@mcnasset.com>"
#   REMINDER_FROM_COMMISSION="MCN Asset <billing@mcnasset.com>"
#
# Verify micana.asia later and only the addresses change; the names stay.
#
# A free mailbox can never be the From address — nobody can prove they own
# gmail.com — which is why the reply-to is what puts the answer in the mailbox
# somebody actually reads. Each company answers its own post:
#
#   REMINDER_REPLY_TO_TMS_RENT / _MICANA_PAYOUT   micana.my@gmail.com
#   REMINDER_REPLY_TO_COMMISSION                  mcn.asset@gmail.com
#
# REMINDER_FROM and REMINDER_REPLY_TO are the fallback for any stream with no
# override of its own.

# The live switch. Any value other than "true" means dry run.

# Do not write to the same person about the same charge more than once this
# often. Defaults to 7 days.

# Ceiling on one run, so a bad query cannot mail everybody. Defaults to 200.

# Which streams are mailed. Unset means all three, which is why this one is
# not left blank: the factory introducer commission is held back deliberately
# until the introducer records are sorted out, and a deployment that copied a
# blank line would start mailing introducers the day it went live.
#
# Add `commission` back to switch it on again. Nothing else has to change —
# the column, the trigger, the template and the tests are all already there.
#
# Worth remembering when you do: micana_payout and commission are both us
# announcing our own lateness to somebody we owe, which is a different act
# from chasing a tenant who owes us.
